Package: iaxphone
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libpulse0 | libasound2t64 | libasound2
Description: IAX2 softphone for the command line
 iaxphone is a softphone speaking IAX2 (RFC 5456), the Inter-Asterisk
 eXchange protocol of Asterisk, written in Go. It registers with a
 server, places and takes calls in G.711 u-law/A-law, sends and receives
 DTMF, rings locally, and uses the system's sound devices through
 miniaudio (PulseAudio/PipeWire or ALSA).
 .
 This package contains the command line phone: register, call, ping and
 devices commands, meant for scripts and for testing against Asterisk.

Package: iaxphone-gui
Architecture: any
# GLFW loads the X11, Wayland and EGL libraries with dlopen, out of sight
# of dpkg-shlibdeps.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         libx11-6, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxinerama1, libxrandr2, libxxf86vm1,
